WEBVTT

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.540
I'm so tired...

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.500
You're tired?! We're the ones
who went along with your shopping!

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.950
We also went to Troer,
so it wasn't just my shopping...

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.290
But you were a big help, Fuuga. Thank you.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.830
I couldn't catch any of the fourth years,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.450
so I thought maybe I couldn't complete
my limited goods collection.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.580
I'm glad to have been some use!

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.910
You're such a good junior!

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.250
And you have some pretty good muscles!

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.910
Though not as good as mine!

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.160
No... Not at all.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.000
All I do is drag the senior students down...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.250
I'm sorry for getting so
worked up in the last match.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.450
I made fouls and stuff...

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.410
That's why we lost
in that last match, right?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.790
This is the last year of
university rugby for all of you...

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.330
I can't believe we can't go to nationals
if we lose the next game...

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.830
I know this sounds cliché,
but it wasn't your fault.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.290
I-It's true! We really think that.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.910
That's right. This is a team game.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.540
No single person is at fault.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.700
What the hell? Why do you all
look so gloomy?!

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.080
This is the best part of rugby!

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.040
We need to overcome these feelings
of self-fault and frustration,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.790
help our teammates, defeat our opponents,
and feel great winning!

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.040
Doesn't everyone play rugby because of that?!

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.000
Well, you have a valid point...

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.580
This pinch we're in is just
the foreplay before our victory.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.450
Since we've been backed into a corner,
winning against Koufuuin for the first time

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.200
can't be any sweeter!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.660
And we're going to do that as a team!

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:54.080
I can't even imagine how amazing
that's going to feel!

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.660
Ren-<i>san</i>! I feel so moved right now!

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.870
We'll definitely win the next match!

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.410
Thank you very much for your coaching!

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.700
I'm jealous of Ren and his way of thinking...

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:09.080
Yeah. That's why you can't really hate him
even though he makes you cringe.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.410
Of course! Everything is
all thanks to my muscles!

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:14.910
What do muscles have to do with it?

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.910
I wonder if Ren will really
make it professionally...

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.910
He's so cringey that I'm worried...

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.750
I hope he finds a team that
realizes his good points, too.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:28.040
Come to think of it, Ikuto was asking if
Thailand was okay for our graduation trip.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.870
You're going to Thailand?!
That sounds so nice!

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.410
I should train my muscles more for the trip!

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.330
What do muscles have to do with the trip?

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.080
I train my muscles even if we go on a vacation!

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.660
Isn't that the kind of man I am?

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.000
No. I have no idea
what kind of man you are!

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.660
I don't want to go.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.870
I don't really like the ocean...

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.830
Why don't you guys go on your own?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.330
You should take this chance
and come with us, Yuuki.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.250
Yeah!

00:02:54.250 --> 00:03:00.200
We both got jobs in the Kansai region,
so we won't be able to see the others often!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.120
Don't worry! I will go
visit you guys from Kanto!

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.750
Isn't that the kind of man I am?

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.540
I told you, I got no idea!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.910
You're planning to go professional,
so I don't think you'll have the time for that.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.040
Shinya, too.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.830
It's not like we won't get any breaks.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.410
Yeah! And there are a lot of
tournaments in the Kansai region!

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.830
We'll be sure to get tickets for you!

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.370
Isn't that the kind of man I am?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.450
I'm seriously going to kick your ass!

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.500
Well, I'm going to excuse myself now.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.500
You're going to go visit Takumi, right?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.450
Yes! With all the first years
that are still here in Kyoto!

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.290
Is Kureha doing okay?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:41.580
He must be feeling a lot of pressure
replacing Hidaka as a starting member...

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.910
H-He's fine! Please don't worry!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.790
Leave Kotori to us first years!

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.950
Seniors, please focus on
your own plays without worry!

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.370
Okay! We're depending on you guys!

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.830
So, it's pretty bad...

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.620
"Chicken tempura tastes the best
right after being fried."

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.870
"Chicken tempura tastes the best
right after being fried."
Natsusa?! What are you doing here?

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.290
Natsusa?! What are you doing here?

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.870
Right back at you, Madoka-<i>san</i>!

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.290
We went to a memorial service.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.830
Right, Kazutaka?

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:37.830
Yeah.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.950
You're so carefree.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.330
Huh? What? Why are you here?!

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.410
Oww.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.290
You're too noisy, Ibuki.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.750
Shoot.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.160
Stay asleep! You two are dangerous together!

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:03.290
Oh! Long time no see, Ibuki stalker.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.410
Ah?

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.750
Hey, now! Don't fight!

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.080
It'll get super troublesome!

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:07.410
"Reiwa"
It'll get super troublesome!

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:09.830
"Reiwa"
He's the only troublesome one here.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.910
"Reiwa"
What are you talking about?

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:12.750
Stop it!

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:15.750
Dealing with your battles right after
waking up will cause me heartburn!

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:19.160
Pretty much as much heartburn as
chugging an entire bottle of sesame oil!

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.290
Seriously, give me a break!

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.580
Oh! Yasunari-<i>kun </i>and Shingyouji are here, too!

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.540
Shingyouji, did you get your touch back?

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.450
Looks like you were pretty messed up last time.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.040
I'm fine now.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:34.950
I see.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.700
I can't wait.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.700
You were always a reserve player
when our teams played in a match,

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.370
so I've never been able to play against you.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:47.040
Don't bully Sei!

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.290
Huh? I'm not bullying him.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.700
That hurts!

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.660
He doesn't like that.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:56.750
Huh? Really?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.700
I think he actually enjoys it a lot.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.370
Of course I don't!

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:01.950
Madoka!

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.040
Ikuto!

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.160
Whoa! Gakuto is here, too!

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.500
It's the Toto pair!

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.250
Oh, stop! That nickname!

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.870
"Oita Sweets"

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.370
What were you doing in Oita?

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.870
Sightseeing!

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.410
Really? How was Oita?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.790
Can I sit here?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.540
Sure. You should turn the seat around!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.660
Kazutaka!

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:26.200
Don't fight and come over here!

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.620
Yeah! Go over there for now!

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.160
Madoka, have you decided which
pro team you're going to sign with?

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.290
Huh? I didn't tell you?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.080
I'm not going pro.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.790
Huh?! No way!

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.330
Even though you had some
great teams try and recruit you?!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.830
You turned them all down?! Why?

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.370
Why?

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:53.830
I think that life other than rugby
seems pretty interesting, too.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:55.790
Where are you going to work?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.950
Oh, I'm not planning on getting a job, either.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.290
For now, I was thinking of
doing some backpacking.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.700
Your big brother is still
such a free spirit, Kazutaka-<i>kun</i>.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.620
I've already given up on him.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.200
But you're not going pro either, Ikuto.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.370
Why?

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.120
Did you feel like you've reached a wall?

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:19.450
Yeah, to put it bluntly.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.160
I get it!

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.160
It's true that I'm a genius at rugby,

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:29.790
but I can't give my life to it
like Kazutaka can.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:33.370
What's the point of being a genius
at rugby if you quit rugby?

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.950
Why did you play rugby
since middle school, then?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.120
What? There was meaning to it.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.540
I love the team building concept in rugby,

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.790
so I'm thinking of making
use of it in the future.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.830
Each player's position is
clearly different in rugby, right?

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:55.370
However, each person works for the team
and the team works for each person.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:59.870
I think this way of thinking is
really useful in the business world.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.120
You're just pulling that
out of your ass, aren't you?

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.830
You found me out?

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:09.370
Meaning? The meaning of playing rugby?

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.700
That was fun!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.080
Well, see you guys on the field!

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:19.500
See you!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.750
I'm going to go talk to him.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.410
Go on without me.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.000
Ikuto.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.790
Are you all right?

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.870
Huh?! Oh!

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.790
Yeah! I'm fine!

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:39.200
Kazutaka!

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:46.080
Hey, Kazutaka. Let's stop this! Please?

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:49.500
I'm sorry for breaking my promise
to go to Koufuuin with you,

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:53.000
but you know my family situation
is pretty complicated, right?

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.370
It couldn't be helped.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:59.750
You really love saying
"it can't be helped," don't you?

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.540
Oh, you're right...

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.910
I keep saying it without realizing it.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.870
What a pathetic guy.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.200
Then, let's do this!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:13.450
Forgive me if we win
against you in the next match.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.290
Who plans to win against who?

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:23.540
Me against you.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.450
Are you being serious?

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:32.120
Yeah. I had given up on making up with you,
but I'm not going to give up anymore.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:33.660
I see.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:38.790
You were so pitiful that I was thinking of
crushing you to end your misery.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:43.750
But now I'll beat you down so badly that
you'll never say such cocky things again.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.160
Feel free, feel free. If you can, that is.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.450
But, if you lose,

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.830
you're going to treat me to some
grilled meat as proof we've made up.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.830
Then, what'll you do if you lose?

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.700
Will you kowtow in front of me?

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.540
Of course, that still won't be
enough for me to forgive you.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:04.000
Okay. Looks like it's a deal.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.250
Brace yourself.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:10.000
I can't wait for that grilled meat!

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:16.370
What'd you provoke him for, Ibuki?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.160
I'm not getting involved.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:21.750
You were provoking Seiichirou,
weren't you, Madoka-<i>san</i>?

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.910
I couldn't help it...

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:28.750
Let me be clear. I really do
want to patch things up.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:33.040
I want to get along with
Natsusa and Shingyouji, too!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.450
Doesn't look like it to me.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:40.160
I'm sorry that we're both terrible
at expressing our affection.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:42.410
Seriously...

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.250
What'd you say?!

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:50.370
I said that it's pointless to
practice tackling and step work.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.620
Why are you so sure it's pointless?!

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:56.500
That's because there's no point
you'd be tackling or using step work.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:00.250
A weak tackle like that
won't even budge your opponent.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.080
And half-assed step work like that
won't get you past them.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:08.410
To begin with, a new number 9 won't be
doing any attack plays in this match.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.830
Are you looking down on college rugby?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.450
I'm not looking down on it at all!

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:14.620
Stop it, Kotori!

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:17.200
And your words are too harsh, Natsu-<i>senpai</i>!

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.290
But it's the truth.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:23.370
If you have time to practice attack plays,
you should be practicing passes more.

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:26.330
Oh! You're not thinking of
getting a try, are you?

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.500
That's impossible. Don't do unnecessary things!

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:34.580
You have such a small frame, so hurry up
and come to terms with what you can do!

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.450
Wh-What's wrong?!

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:38.290
Kotori!

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.410
Shut up! Don't call me by my first name!

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:44.040
Natsusa-<i>san </i>really pisses people off, huh?

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.790
Yasunari! You bastard! Are you
talking bad about Natsu-<i>senpai</i>?!

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:52.620
But he pisses you off
because it's the truth, right?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:57.040
He tells you the things you don't want to hear.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.620
Shut up!

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.040
I was the same way.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:05.290
It pissed me off when
Natsusa-<i>san </i>poked at my complex.

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:12.410
But I think that both you and I
want to overcome our complexes.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.750
Am I right?

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:20.370
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.750
I want to get strong.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:28.750
Strong enough to prove everyone who
calls me small and weak that they're wrong!

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.660
I'm going to say, "Take that!" to them!

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.540
They made up!

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.000
Huh?

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.700
Huh? Really?

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.450
I mean, it means that they
have the same goal, right?

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:42.750
That makes them comrades!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.540
I see! So that's how it is!

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.410
Huh? No...

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.200
We're not...

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:53.120
Now that you two have made up,
the first years should all go eat together!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.120
Wow! That makes me so happy!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.080
We're all eating together!

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:02.250
You're right! We never got together
since you two were always fighting!

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:06.910
Let's hurry up and go! Yasunari-<i>kun</i>! Koto... Ah!

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.500
You can't, Yuu!

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.080
You should let it slide, Koto... Ah!

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:15.540
Just to be clear, those two
aren't doing it on purpose.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.040
I know...

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.870
Go ahead and call me Kotori...

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.290
Really?! You're so kind, Koto...

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.450
You never got it, either way!

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:29.870
Ta-da!

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.120
Whoa! What's this?

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:35.790
Aren't they cute? Take one you like!

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:38.830
I like this one. Looks like the Tigers!

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:44.200
You know, I've always wondered whether
he liked rugby or baseball more.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:48.000
Let's see. Is there a design that doesn't
pale in comparison to my muscles?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.040
Makoto, maybe you'd like this one?

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.120
I'm okay with picking after everyone else.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.330
I-I can't keep something this flashy...

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:57.790
Liar!

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:01.370
You were wearing a t-shirt
with a super flashy girl on it last time!

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.540
Moka-<i>chan </i>is my girl!

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:07.950
It would be rude to even consider
flashiness when buying her goods!

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:10.910
I really don't get the reasons
that piss off an otaku!

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:14.910
Oh, I already made the reservations
for our graduation trip.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.790
You can't cancel, Yuuki.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.000
I-I know...

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.200
I never thought there'd be a day that
all of us would go on a trip together.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:26.410
I agree. We didn't get along at all in the past.

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:30.540
Someone would be punching it out
with another at least every other week.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.000
Yeah, it was really scary.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.200
You idiot. You were the scariest!

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.250
Huh?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:39.290
You started throwing punches because
I accidentally stepped on your pin!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:39.910
"Doesn't it frustrate you?"
"I'm rooting for you, meow!!"
You started throwing punches because
I accidentally stepped on your pin!

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:45.830
"Doesn't it frustrate you?"
"I'm rooting for you, meow!!"
That was a limited edition Moka-<i>chan </i>pin
I finally got from the gacha machine!

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:49.080
No, no. Akkun had the shortest temper.

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:52.950
You're the only guy who would punch someone
just because they said your name.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:56.200
It's their fault for calling me by name
when I told them not to.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.790
You were all so violent back then.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.830
It would have been really bad
if there wasn't a mediator like me.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.250
Mediator?!

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.830
To be honest, I hated you the most!

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:11.200
Ren-<i>san </i>is the hardest to handle
if you aren't used to him.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.660
Why?!

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.500
Oh, I see!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.120
Were you jealous of my muscles?!

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.000
It's that part about you.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.410
Can I say something?

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.250
Gakuto, what is it?

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.330
I wrote a letter.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.660
I'm going to read it here,
so I'd like you all to listen.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.620
A letter?!

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.870
Is it about my faults?!

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:39.580
If you tell me something like that,
I won't be able to play in the next match!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.410
No, it's nothing like that.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:47.200
Our captain does some
really surprising things sometimes...

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:48.950
Well, let's listen for now.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:53.200
"To all the fourth years.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.870
Until now, I have left things to Ikuto

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:59.160
and have not expressed my feelings much.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:05.790
I wrote this letter to express my feelings
to everyone about the Kansai League.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:10.290
I was told by Ikuto that I was
the best captain he's ever had in Oita,

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:12.830
but I do not believe that is the case.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.040
I believe I am the worst of all captains."

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.250
That's not true at all!

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:22.080
"Because I am not good with my words
and I lack the attention to detail,

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.790
I have been unable to bring the
third years and first years together.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:32.040
I have put such a talented team in danger of
being eliminated in the Kansai League.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.410
This has never happened before.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:36.950
I cannot call myself a good captain.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:43.290
Even so, the reason I remain captain is
because all of you have stayed by my side.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.750
I don't think it was easy.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:50.370
In the end, only four of us have remained
in the starting line-up in our last year.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.450
I am sure many of you are frustrated,

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:55.870
uneasy, and unsatisfied by various things.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:01.700
Even so, thank you for still calling me captain.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.500
Thank you for supporting me."

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:10.450
S-Stop it. You make it sound like
this is going to be our last match...

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:12.750
That is why I want to win.

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:17.450
If we lose here, I am definitely
the worst of captains.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:22.120
I cannot allow a captain that you have
supported like this embarrass you.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.290
We will definitely win.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.330
You're really such a great guy!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.080
We'll definitely win this week!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:34.250
Captain! I have always thought of you
as captain the moment I saw your pecs!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:38.120
Liar! You were totally planning on
being captain in the beginning!

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.870
Akkun, you, too...

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:45.250
I remember Yuuki trying to become captain
to change our uniforms to Moka-<i>chan</i>...

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.950
That's because we have
Moka-<i>chan</i>'s color scheme!

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:52.080
We could do it for our juniors! We could
even make it in time for the next match!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.580
I think we shouldn't for
the sake of our juniors...

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:55.750
I agree.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:58.080
--Ikuto.
--Not everyone is a fan of Moka-chan!

00:18:58.080 --> 00:18:59.750
Are you all right?

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.000
Yeah...

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:08.290
So is that replica uniform of mine yours now?

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.580
That's right. It looks better on me.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.750
I can lend it to you every once in a while.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:16.290
I see. I had really liked it a lot...

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.950
Right, Mikan?

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:21.540
Mikan has such a bad personality!

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:23.660
It's because you spoil him, Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>!

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:26.750
Those with the same personality tend to clash...

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:28.750
What is that supposed to mean?

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:32.040
Oh! Seiichirou is just eating
the chicken tempura again!

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:35.580
Oh! You're right! Sei,
don't just eat the chicken tempura!

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:39.580
Come to think of it, Kazutaka really liked
Natsusa's chicken tempura, too.

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:44.620
Why did the two of you
suddenly stop being friends?

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.330
You two were always together in high school.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:49.660
Hm?

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:53.660
I-I'm sorry. I'm not trying to pry.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:56.700
It's okay. I'll tell you in his place.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:20:00.830
Our weak-minded god, Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>,
and a tragic heroine wanna-be

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:03.700
created a selfish campfire with
the members of the Ueoka family

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.330
that created a miracle collaboration

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:09.580
which caused him to break his
promise with Kazutaka-<i>san</i>...

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.830
What does that mean?

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:17.200
It's a story about a god and a heroine
that created a miracle from a campfire?

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:24.160
Well, in other words, I was supposed to
go to Koufuuin and play with Kazutaka,

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:31.120
but my family, mainly my older brothers,
suddenly prevented me from enrolling.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:35.660
Oh, I had also thought you
were going to Koufuuin...

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:39.830
I was surprised to find out that you
went to Doushisha after graduating.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:44.120
Huh?! You looked so uninterested
when I said I was changing universities,

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.000
but you were actually surprised?

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.790
N-Not really!

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:49.160
Anyway!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.450
He won't forgive me
no matter how much I apologize!

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:55.290
He won't even listen to what happened!

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:59.120
I didn't end up doing something
like that because I wanted to!

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:03.410
I understand Kazutaka-<i>san</i>'s feelings.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:07.790
If someone did that to me without coming
to me after we had promised for so long,

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.660
I would be mad, too.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.080
No! You know I didn't even have
time to talk it over with him!

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.410
I know.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:19.120
But if Natsu did something like that to me,
getting angry wouldn't be enough.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:23.160
Please don't suddenly go psychopath on me.

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.450
By the way, where is Yayoi and the others?

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:30.200
If they're coming,
I'll start frying another round.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:33.830
W-Well, they decided not to come today.

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.500
Kotori-<i>kun </i>is... Um...

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:40.370
Well, Yayoi-<i>kun </i>and Saitou-<i>kun</i>
are with Kotori-<i>kun </i>and...

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:44.410
Huh?! Kotori ended up hating me that much?!

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:46.120
Of course he did...

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.830
Th-That's not true!

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:54.080
Just, Kotori-<i>kun</i>... Uh!
Meeting you, right now is... Um...

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.790
He kind of wants to prove you wrong! Kind of...

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.160
The three of them are going over
Koufuuin videos right now!

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.040
Please be at ease!

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.910
Then, I'll fry up the rest after all.

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:06.410
Huh?

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:09.290
They should cool down
by the time you go home, Yuu.

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:12.120
I'll wrap them up and you can bring it to them.

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:14.500
Yes!

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:17.250
The feelings of people are hard to understand...

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:42.000
"Victory at the Kansai League!!"

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:45.200
"When watching rugby in winter,
dress as warmly as possible!!"
I-I know it may be too late, but since
the preview comments keep getting cut-off,

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:47.000
"When watching rugby in winter,
dress as warmly as possible!!"
I will try my best to finish!
